ENV/
# .python-version is deliberately NOT ignored here: `services/api/.python-version`
# pins the project's shared Python version (3.13, matching
# `pyproject.toml`'s `requires-python`) for every contributor and CI —
# a committed configuration file, not a per-developer pyenv preference.
# The generic Python .gitignore template this section was based on
# assumes the opposite (a personal, uncommitted pin) and was wrong for
# this repo's actual convention.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytype/
.pyre/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.so
.installed.cfg
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Machine learning / data
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.onnx
*.safetensors
.mlflow/
wandb/
.keras/
dvc.lock
dvc.yaml
.dvc/
# Anchored to the repo root: these are meant to ignore local ML-tooling
# scratch output (e.g. MLflow/DVC run directories), not any directory that
# happens to share the name deeper in the tree — unanchored patterns here
# previously shadowed real source (apps/dashboard/src/features/experiments/,
# the (dashboard)/experiments/ route, services/api/tests/experiments/,
# services/api/app/models/ — see services/api/.gitignore's own note on
# the last one). Every rule in this block is deliberately root-scoped for
# the same reason; none of them should ever be widened back to a bare,
# unanchored `name/` pattern.
/runs/
/experiments/
/models/

/artifacts/
/datasets/
*.parquet.tmp*

